# v1.0.1

## Features
[feature] OneDrop is its own app — send any file to a nearby phone or PC, and keep listening in the background
[feature] Photos picker and Files browser (same FileExplorer as MessageMe) sit on the home send actions
[feature] Incoming photos can go in the camera roll or Pictures/OneDrop; documents stay in the files folder
[feature] Photos picker splits Camera roll from Other folders, with Photos / Videos / Favorites / Screenshots chips
[feature] On Windows and other desktops, Open folder shows the OneDrop inbox in File Explorer, and Settings can open it once when a drop arrives
[feature] Installers for every client: Android APK, Windows zip with onedrop.exe, Ubuntu .deb, Ubuntu Touch, and separate Apple Silicon and Intel Mac disk images

## Improvements
[improvement] Each file can be up to about 7 GB — enough for a long 4K clip or an ISO
[improvement] The home-screen icon is the OneDrop family teardrop, not a blank tile
[improvement] Nearby uses the phone name or computer name automatically — no “name this PC” screen
[improvement] On the phone, back-swipe stays in OneDrop instead of closing the app
[improvement] Phone Settings uses the same full-size cards and choices as other AmL apps
[improvement] Phone home drop is a smaller glassy teardrop with no clipped corner, and the tap hint sits a little higher above Photos and Files
[improvement] Phone home drop sits in the middle of expanding circular waves
[improvement] Nearby device circles show Phone, PC, Mac, or Linux instead of an initial
[improvement] Nearby device labels are lighter and sit smaller in the circle
[improvement] The Windows panel centers a small droplet with OneDrop and the version, instead of the bird and header title
[improvement] Photos picker chips are pastel and readable, and shrink together on small phones
[improvement] Photos picker loads the thumbs on screen first when you scroll past the top
[improvement] Files picker uses a Send button, and New folder only shows when choosing a receive folder
[improvement] Video thumbs in the Photos picker show clip length in a white knockout bubble, like chat
[improvement] Photos picker groups camera photos under Camera roll, not Gallery
[improvement] Photos picker title follows the selected chip — All, Photos, Videos, Favorites, or Screenshots
[improvement] Home send tile and hint say Media files, and the hint says tap the droplet

## Bug fixes
[bugfix] Receiving shows Cancel, so a stuck 0% drop on Windows can be dismissed
[bugfix] Photos picker lists the camera roll newest-first, not a mixed Recents album
[bugfix] Photos picker Favorites shows loved photos and videos the way Gallery Loved does, instead of a single clip
[bugfix] Cancel on “Waiting for them to accept” leaves that screen immediately
[bugfix] Back-swipe on phone Settings returns to Home instead of leaving the app
[bugfix] Back-swipe on phone Home stays in OneDrop instead of leaving the app
[bugfix] This phone no longer appears as a nearby Wi-Fi device when Gallery’s One Drop is also running
